  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+4y=2.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t+\u03d5)+2$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t+\u03d5)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n- $y={e}^{-t}(A\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $\u03d5$ are constants.",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{\u2033}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$\nIt can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=4\\,\u27f9\\,\\omega =2.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ Since the external force is a constant, we assume that the particular solution is also a constant,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t+\u03d5)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t+\u03d5)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nOnly II match the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
